1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,620
The decision was taken around a warm table in the family house.

2
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:13,019
His mom invited both families, and the debate that followed was, in her words, a lot of fun and very tense.

3
00:00:13,019 --> 00:00:16,878
“He will tell you what happened,” she said.

4
00:00:16,878 --> 00:00:23,202
“I will say only this: the marital contract is not the marriage.”

5
00:00:23,202 --> 00:00:26,252
The beginning of the meeting was formal.

6
00:00:26,252 --> 00:00:34,961
A motion was proposed, a request for a triple enhancement of the schedule, and a nod from the head of the table.

7
00:00:34,961 --> 00:00:39,261
“Apply for the money,” the fatherly uncle said.

8
00:00:39,261 --> 00:00:47,100
“Beg if you must, but do not borrow.” “Do not panic,” the motherly aunt added.

9
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:54,709
“The concern of the woman who raised the child has been received, and at home it is great.”

10
00:00:54,709 --> 00:01:07,388
There was a demonstrative moment: the beloved grandmother borrowed a pen, signed the paper, and put it down with a slap that disposed of three months of spite in one second.

11
00:01:07,388 --> 00:01:19,207
“The scent of a new plan is better than the curse of an old quarrel,” she said, and the talkative cousin, for once, said nothing at all.

12
00:01:19,207 --> 00:01:23,451
The divorce of the two projects had begun quietly.

13
00:01:23,451 --> 00:01:30,370
One would continue; the other would be transmitted to a replacement who could give it more time.

14
00:01:30,370 --> 00:01:33,115
“I know,” Lin said.

15
00:01:33,115 --> 00:01:45,424
“I like the little one better.” A steep fall in his own hours had taught him that, and the plunging temperature outside made the kitchen feel like a harbor.

16
00:01:45,424 --> 00:01:51,003
The wonder was that the decision had been reached without anyone raising a voice.

17
00:01:51,003 --> 00:02:02,161
The steamy windows, the warm plates, the little indications that people were still there: everything indicated a family that had decided something.

18
00:02:02,161 --> 00:02:06,916
“Something has to commence,” the cousin finally said.

19
00:02:06,916 --> 00:02:24,679
“Call it a fancy name if you like; the people are the same people.” Some of it was luck, and some of it was the part nobody had planned: the cousin's silence, the aunt's arithmetic, the way a family decides without deciding.

20
00:02:24,679 --> 00:02:35,604
They had spent a month on the schedule and one evening on the marriage, which was, in the end, the correct proportion of the two.
